## Page Boilerplate
<!-- The exact top-of-file PHP + outer HTML skeleton every public page follows. Include the literal include() order and any required session/ini calls. This is the single most-copied chunk in the project — pin it down precisely. -->

## File Structure & Folder Roles
<!-- What lives where and why. Cover: which files sit at the root, what each subfolder is for (includes/, functions/, per-feature subtrees), and any conventions like redirect-stub index.php in non-public folders. -->

## Database & Globals
<!-- PDO connection style (charset, error mode, env switching), how the connection handle is named and shared, multi-tenant filters, prepared-statement style (positional vs named), fetch idioms (FETCH_ASSOC loops, fetchColumn for counts, rowCount gating), input pre-filtering before binding, and which globals are defined in the connection file. -->

## Routing & Clean URLs
<!-- The mapping from clean URLs to .php targets, where rewrites are expected (.htaccess, server config, neither), and the convention for "not found" outcomes (redirect to a 404 page vs http_response_code). -->

## Page Meta & SEO
<!-- How per-page title/description/OG/Twitter/canonical/robots are set: dictionary lookup, direct global assignment, or both. List the exact variable names. Note JSON-LD blocks emitted per page type and pagination/robots rules (e.g. NOINDEX on page 2+). -->

## Shared Includes
<!-- The fixed set of layout fragments (preloader, header, footer, search modal, sidebar, etc.), their include order, which globals each depends on, and the path style for nested pages (./includes vs ../includes). -->

## Reusable Helpers
<!-- PHP helper functions defined once and used across pages: card renderers, pagination, truncation, formatters, IP/session helpers. For each: signature, what it emits, where it's typically called from. -->

## Form Handling
<!-- The end-to-end form recipe: CSRF token render/validate, honeypot, input filtering (regex per field type), submit dispatch (by button name), session-key dedupe, POST → Redirect → GET, where the handler sits relative to the markup. -->

## Security Conventions
<!-- session.cookie_httponly, redirect-stub index.php in non-public folders, character-class input filtering, CSRF on every POST, any other defensive habits that aren't covered above. -->

